~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
Jory: Oh — hey. Didn't hear you come up. Boat, was it? Nobody comes by boat any more.
Jory: Welcome to Hearth Hollow, friend. Old fishing town. Abandoned, mostly — the fish went, then the boats, then the people. A few of us stayed. I like the quiet.
Jory: So. What brings you all this way? What's your purpose here?
Traveller: Just heading through.
Jory: Ah. See, that's the thing — you can't. The road out, up past the trees and over the ridge, got blocked off years back. Barricaded, signed, the lot. Nobody's been through since.
Traveller: But I have to.
Jory: Ha. Everyone who washes up here says that. [wait=0.6] Alright. Go and speak to the Blacksmith. Up past the meadow, the big house with the chimney — you'll hear the hammer before you see him.
Jory: He's an odd one, fair warning. But if anyone can get you through, it's him.
Jory: And take a moment to explore while you're at it. There's more of the town left than it looks. The hut on the north shore, the woods. Nobody'll mind. Nobody's here to.
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END

~ again
do start_talking()
Jory: [[Blacksmith's up past the meadow. Follow the hammer.|Road's still blocked, friend. Still.|Have a wander. The hut on the north shore's worth a look.|I'd offer you a tune, but you look like a man with somewhere to be.]]
do stop_talking()
=> END
